      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Consider analyzing the precise timing and load on the physical or virtual host running your Jenkins agent. Look for underlying infrastructure issues like periodic garbage collection pauses in the JVM, disk I/O bottlenecks, or transient networking hiccups that are hard to reproduce locally. Sometimes, background cluster maintenance or anti-virus scans on the host machine can introduce these sporadic, invisible interruptions.",
      "source": "target",
